  <p class="note-line">
    IITs and NITs almost universally require Mathematics through JEE for every branch, biotechnology included. A plain PCB student without Maths generally cannot access those specific seats. Bio-Maths students, or PCB students at universities that run a maths bridge course, have a genuinely wider set of B.Tech doors than students believe.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>A B.Tech label does not automatically pay an engineering-scale salary in these branches.</strong>
